Description: fdrv/bsp: range-check firmware-supplied message ids and vif/sta/chan indices
 Message ids and vif/station/channel indices in firmware E2A messages
 and rx descriptors are used as array indices without range checks.
 Validate them against their table sizes before dispatch and drop
 messages that fail; bound the handler-table lookup in fdrv and bsp;
 check sta_idx/dst_idx and vlan_idx in the rx data path.
 .
 SM_CONNECT_IND only has its ap/ch/width indices checked when
 status_code is 0, since the handler only uses them on success and a
 failed connect must still be reported. SCANU_RESULT_IND also requires
 ind->length to cover the probe response fixed fields
 (offsetof(struct ieee80211_mgmt, u.probe_resp.variable)), which the
 handler reads unconditionally.
Author: N Oliver <3945917+PixnBits@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-26
